==== a module the base suppresses
# apps/flatpak

Installs flatpak and enables the remotes an image asks for

## Where it is built

Nowhere. suppressed lists it and builds no layer for it: everything it provides, that base already ships.

## What it exchanges

| Direction | What | With |
| --- | --- | --- |
| provides | `flatpak` | apps/browser |

## What it declares to install

| Family | Packages | Enabled repository |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `fedora` | `flatpak` | default |

## What it claims

| Benchmark | Rules |
| --- | --- |
| `cis-fedora` | 9.9.9.9 |

A claim the tool records rather than certifies. The scan is what confirms it.

## Where it came from

| Content | Hash |
| --- | --- |
| declared | `d40c2891d1aac415c97068412a248e05aaea222ab467ca113436d3954d4d6467` |

It was written in this repository rather than imported, so nothing upstream to compare it against.

## What it pulls in

Nothing. It declares no `asset`.

## Third-party repositories

None. It declares no `copr` and ships no `repo` file.

